-- Licence: CC BY 4.0. Attribution is required wherever these boundaries
--          are drawn, and is carried in the wards table so any report or
--          export can cite it without anyone remembering to.
--
-- Coordinates are rounded to six decimal places, about 11 centimetres,
-- which is far finer than a ward boundary is surveyed to and cuts the file
-- to something you can paste into the SQL editor.
--
-- One feature in the source file is deliberately NOT loaded: Ward_No 0,
-- zone "St. Thomas Mount". That is a cantonment board, not a GCC ward, and
-- including it would make Chennai read as 201 wards and quietly skew every
-- coverage percentage computed against the total.
--
-- Idempotent: re-running replaces the geometry for a ward it already has.
-- Depends on: ward-density.sql.
-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

